is he going to do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, he does happen to be capable of consuming ghostly essence in place of vitae - could he steal an animal ghost's form like one might do from consuming animal blood?<br /> Time for experiment number 1. The really bizarre stuff comes <i><b>after</b></i> he manages to pull that off, if even feasible. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cross-a-way</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1528022-immortal-hobbies?p=1529684#post1529684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">also does he realize how much food a mammoth would need?</div> </div> </div> </div>One step at a time - check on how viable replication might be in the first place. He's in it as much for the journey as any hypothetical prize in the end...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-30T12:05:47-08:00","id":1529725,"title":"","content":"Ordo Dracul always experimenting to the bitter end.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-30T14:00:39-08:00","id":1529735,"title":"","content":"I wonder how many vampires are around that petted mammoths the first time. Probably not many, that was pre sundering but maybe some.<br /> <br /> ETA: I was wrong, it was apparently several thousand years post sundering that they went extinct. Maybe some Gangrel didn't just let a wooly mammoth, maybe they petted Wooly Mammoth. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.nhm.ac.uk/discover/last-mammoths.html#:~:text=Woolly%20mammoths%20roamed%20parts%20of,years%20ago%20they%20were%20gone\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.nhm.ac.uk/discover/last-...%20were%20gone</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","user":"ShadowcatX","date":". 01-30-2024, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-30T16:20:28-08:00","id":1529740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1528022-immortal-hobbies?p=1529735#post1529735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how many vampires are around that petted mammoths the first time. Probably not many, that was pre sundering but maybe some.<br /> <br /> ETA: I was wrong, it was apparently several thousand years post sundering that they went extinct. Maybe some Gangrel didn't just let a wooly mammoth, maybe they petted Wooly Mammoth.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.nhm.ac.uk/discover/last-mammoths.html#:~:text=Woolly%20mammoths%20roamed%20parts%20of,years%20ago%20they%20were%20gone\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.nhm.ac.uk/discover/last-...%20were%20gone</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's a NPC archetype in the OD book that half-implies it might secretly be a remnant of the last glaciation period, so i'd say possible indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-30T19:00:42-08:00","id":1529741,"title":"","content":"Architetect of Shards, they research an era's customs, aesthetics, technology, construction style, etc. They build a mansion, castle or even village depending on their vampire client, tailored to be a replica of their home time, an island of nostalgia in the sea of time. They only take projects they find interesting or challenging.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T19:50:28-07:00","id":1532630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1528022-immortal-hobbies?p=1529735#post1529735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how many vampires are around that petted mammoths the first time. Probably not many, that was pre sundering but maybe some.<br /> <br /> ETA: I was wrong, it was apparently several thousand years post sundering that they went extinct. Maybe some Gangrel didn't just let a wooly mammoth, maybe they petted Wooly Mammoth.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.nhm.ac.uk/discover/last-mammoths.html#:~:text=Woolly%20mammoths%20roamed%20parts%20of,years%20ago%20they%20were%20gone\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.nhm.ac.uk/discover/last-...%20were%20gone</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I like about Requiem; you can actually have a near-immortal character, that's thousands of years old, even old enough to pet a mammoth, but not have to explain why they're 2nd Generation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T12:13:37-07:00","id":1532715,"title":"","content":"I wonder how many immortals having clear memories of famous historical figures they might have encountered or knew or if they remember where precisely where their childhood homes might be after the passage of so much time? I remember some trivia from Highlander the series when Duncan meets Methos and the ancient immortal admits that his life before his immortality is very fuzzy to say the least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 03-20-2024, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T15:08:02-07:00","id":1532726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1528022-immortal-hobbies?p=1532715#post1532715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how many immortals having clear memories of famous historical figures they might have encountered or knew or if they remember where precisely where their childhood homes might be after the passage of so much time? I remember some trivia from Highlander the series when Duncan meets Methos and the ancient immortal admits that his life before his immortality came is very fuzzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Add to that the element of Torpor for some potential twists. If just one night of sleep can sometimes so rattle a person she wakes uncertain of the line between fact and delirium, what to say of the fact vampires will sometimes sleep, perchance dream, not for a few hours but whole days, weeks, months, years or lifetimes - how may such further muddle the whole of the morass that is a restless dead's memory? And that without going into the extra potential complication of any possible supernatural heft such &quot;dreams of the dead&quot; might develop due to a variety of circunstances. That's quite the slippery slope in potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-17T14:04:33-07:00","id":1532775,"title":"","content":"Certainly in the 1st edition they mentioned that topor can twist memories of Kindred as there desires and fears mesh with what they can recall and you get someone who isn\u2019t sure what happened really went down as they think. The Deava ancient Zagrief was an exception to the rule but I don\u2019t think he ever slept long and at best that there is a century gap in his memory which mildly concerns him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}